<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria offers 5.0 bln levs 2-yr T-notes Friday.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria offers 5.0 bln levs 2-yr T-notes Friday.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry said on Tuesday it will offer five billion levs of fixed interest two-year T-notes with no minimum acceptable price set in advance at an auction on Friday.</p>
<p>Interest on the paper is set at 7.5 percent annually. Coupon payments are due semiannually until maturity and the principal is payable upon maturity.</p>
<p>Of the total par on offer 95 percent are earmarked for competitive bids and the remainder for non-competitive bids.</p>
<p>Details of the offer follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	     BG2042397211</p>
<p> Maturity		   two years</p>
<p> Par value		  5.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	     August 22</p>
<p> Issue date		 August 28</p>
<p> Maturity date	    August 26, 1999</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
</text>
